To create a colorful and interactive website with a real joke replacing the mock-up, you can use HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. Here's a basic outline of the steps:

1. Create a new HTML file and add a container for the joke, such as a `<div>` element.
```html
<div id="joke-container">
  <p id="joke"></p>
</div>
```
1. Add a JavaScript file to the HTML file, which will handle the joke replacement.
```html
<script src="your-javascript-file.js"></script>
```
1. In the JavaScript file, create a function that fetches a joke from an API or a database and replaces the mock-up joke with the real joke.
```javascript
async function fetchJoke() {
  const response = await fetch('https://api.example.com/joke');
  const joke = await response.json();
  document.getElementById('joke').textContent = joke.joke;
}
```
1. Call the `fetchJoke()` function on page load or when the user clicks a button.
```javascript
document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', fetchJoke);
```
1. Style the joke container with CSS to make it colorful and interactive.
```css
#joke-container {
  background-color: #ffcc00;
  padding: 20px;
  border-radius: 10px;
  text-align: center;
}

#joke {
  font-size: 24px;
  margin-bottom: 10px;
}
```
1. Add a button or a link to trigger the joke replacement when clicked.
```html
<button id="joke-button">Get a joke</button>
```
1. Add an event listener to the button or link to call the `fetchJoke()` function when clicked.
```javascript
const jokeButton = document.getElementById('joke-button');
jokeButton.addEventListener('click', fetchJoke);
```
